{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:6b394a54cdf0083e","name":"T'salak Spawn","source":{"id":"source:reference-6b394a54cdf0083e","title":"T'salak Spawn","revision":21758,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:25:50Z","sha256":"c31a28bbdf2999357671f3f077a3e1bd1af96893a15ea123c6a1bf14fe310dad","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21758","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=T%27salak%20Spawn&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-6b394a54cdf0083e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Echoes of the Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Echoes_of_the_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:e6a2e80208e1e351"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["You've seen the effects of this creature's touch, and you certainly don't want to suffer the same fate as those poor souls that you encountered earlier. It seems wiser to skirt around the beast and hope that it doesn't follow."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Force-sensitive creature of unknown origin, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salak","referenceId":"reference:04f3fcf5598f0786"}," is an oozing, black mound of evil. A specimen was first encountered in the jungles of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cularin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cularin"}," and subsequently imprisoned inside a Force-imbued urn. The urn was buried inside a cave and guarded by a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tarasin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tarasin"}," village for generations, until recently stolen by the Dark Jedi ",{"tag":"a","children":["Raik Muun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Raik_Muun","referenceId":"reference:c285787da26dc6dd"},". With the help of scientists, Raik discovered a way to divide the ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salak","referenceId":"reference:04f3fcf5598f0786"}," into independent entities of equal power. It is unknown how many more specimens remain in existence.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salak","referenceId":"reference:04f3fcf5598f0786"}," has no sensory organs but leaves no question as to its strength and cunning; it lashes out with sticky tendrils that have surprising accuracy and power. Filled with chaotic thoughts born of malignity, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["T'salak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T%27salak","referenceId":"reference:04f3fcf5598f0786"}," can induce a blinding rage in its targets just by touching them, permeating their souls with darkness.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Its T'salak Spawn appear to be small pieces that have broken away from the main body. They are weaker and more easily destroyed, but they still impart some madness on their targets.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["T'salak Spawn Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Fo